    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmap\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nmini.map integration highlights do not work. added lines are expected to be green in the map.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/40532058/be30d917-b9f6-43a6-9cd8-87b14dee77f4)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-354+g24b60b0f7 (24b60b0f71e0ffbd09c827230ecb5a37e833cade)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Use this minimal config\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n...\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"catppuccin/nvim\",\r\n\t\tname = \"catppuccin\",\r\n\t\tpriority = 1000,\r\n\t\topts = {\r\n\t\t\tintergration = {\r\n\t\t\t\tmini = true,\r\n\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\tcustom_highlights = function(colors)\r\n\t\t\t\treturn {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tMiniMapNormal = { fg = colors.surface0 },\r\n\t\t\t\t\tMiniMapSymbolCount = { fg = colors.mauve },\r\n\t\t\t\t\tMiniMapSymbolLine = { fg = colors.surface1 },\r\n\t\t\t\t\tMiniMapSymbolView = { fg = colors.surface0 },\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\tend,\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\tconfig = function(_, opts)\r\n\t\t\trequire(\"catppuccin\").setup(opts)\r\n\r\n\t\t\tvim.cmd.colorscheme(\"catppuccin\")\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t},\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim\",\r\n\t\topts = true,\r\n\t},\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.map\",\r\n\t\tversion = false,\r\n\t\tdependencies = \"lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim\",\r\n\t\tlazy = false,\r\n\t\tkeys = { ... },\r\n\t\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\t\tlocal map = require(\"mini.map\")\r\n\t\t\tmap.setup({\r\n\t\t\t\tintegrations = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tmap.gen_integration.gitsigns({\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tadd = \"GitSignsAdd\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tchange = \"GitSignsChange\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tdelete = \"GitSignsDelete\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\t}),\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\tsymbols = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tencode = map.gen_encode_symbols.block(\"3x2\"),\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\twindow = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tshow_integration_count = true,\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t})\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t},\r\n}, {\r\n\tchange_detection = {\r\n\t\tnotify = false,\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Open a tracked file and modify some lines. The highlights are simply not shown. We can doubly check that the integrations do actually exist by running `:= MiniMap.gen_integration.gitsigns()()`, and the highlights are somehow the issue.\r\n\r\nAm i missing something?\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nHighlights are applied to affected minimap lines.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nLines remain on their default highlighting",
